ws out of the SUM source set; (7) ON DELETE CASCADE tenant isolation — deleting orgA via raw SQL CASCADE-removes orgA's quota_reservations rows and leaves orgB's three peers (active services, active projects, committed databases) byte-identical to baseline, mirroring TestQuotaUsageOrganizationDeleteCascadeIsTenantScoped (BE-0454). Helpers introduced: assertQuotaReservationByteIdentical + per-file ptr helpers stringPtrEqualQR/timePtrEqualQR/fmtStringPtrQR/fmtTimePtrQR (per-file QR suffix is mandatory because the package-shared store_test space already exposes QP-suffixed variants from BE-0451). All other helpers reused: seedOrg (schema_test.go), insertReservationRow/insertSettledReservationRow (quota_repository_test.go), loadQuotaReservationRowByID/countQuotaReservationRowsForOrg/runInsertReservationOrFail (BE-0455 invariants). All 7 tests PASS against an isolated migrated Postgres (race-clean, 2.83s). gofmt/vet clean. Pre-existing TestEnvironmentService*, TestAPIKeyServiceCreate*, TestProjectVariableService*, TestOrganizationVariableServicePatch*, TestServiceServiceCreate* parallel-induced flakes reproduce at HEAD without this change (22 failures with the file stashed; same set surfaces with the file in place; BE-0455's commit notes already documented this)."
